What is not here
----------------
No Line 6 firmware, code or data is included or distributed. The build reads
the user's own copy of the official HX Stomp, HX Stomp XL, HX Effects or Helix LT
3.80.0 firmware file and changes
it on the user's computer. The patcher contains the offsets and table layouts
it needs to do that, and checks the input's MD5 first. Firmware built with
it contains Line 6's firmware and should not be redistributed.

No Neural Amp Modeler model files (.nam captures) are included.

Third-party material
--------------------
tools/sharc/sasm.py: the SHARC opcode tables are adapted from
tools/sharc_isa.py of the ghidra-sharc extension
(https://github.com/roblg/ghidra-sharc), licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). That file
transcribes them from the Analog Devices "SHARC Processor Programming
Reference".

tools/effects.py: the HX Effects support builds on Scott's HX Effects port,
hx-effects-nam-lite (https://github.com/scottlynn73/hx-effects-nam-lite,
GPL-3.0-or-later, itself built on this project): the HX Effects' User IR store
and model-table offsets, and taking over a stock model's identity there.

CustomOS (tools/patch_menu.py, tools/features/, tools/m4asm.py,
tools/setting_ids.py, tools/image_store.py, tools/patch_splash.py,
tools/splash_emoji.py, tools/splash_topo.py, tools/emoji_png.swift, src/m4/,
their tests, FIRMWARE_NOTES.md, docs/resource-limits.md): from
wisemandenny's hx-stomp-customOS
(https://github.com/wisemandenny/hx-stomp-customOS, commit 661da72,
GPL-3.0-or-later, itself built on this project), unchanged but for one test's
expected build.py line.

helix-lt/lt_port.py builds on savedadodo's Helix Floor port,
helix-floor-nam-lite (https://github.com/savedadodo/helix-floor-nam-lite,
commit 29aea81, GPL-3.0-or-later): the build runs that port's own code with
the Helix LT's addresses; none of its files are in this repository.

Photo docs/hx-stomp-xl-amp-nam.jpg: Med Hamza, used with credit.

Neural Amp Modeler (https://github.com/sdatkinson/neural-amp-modeler,
MIT licence): src/sharc/nam_a2.asm and tools/sharc/nam_multi_kernel.asm are
independent implementations of the A2 WaveNet arithmetic, written from the
model file format; no NeuralAmpModelerCore source is included.

